          "source": "palm",
          "analysis": "This is an ARM-based DDoS bot. The binary daemonizes itself by forking twice, then connects to a command and control (C2) server. The `main` function enters a loop to receive and process commands via the `processCmd` function. This function parses attack commands such as `UDPRAW`, `RANDHEX`, `STD`, and `OVH`, which trigger corresponding flood functions (`UDPRAW`, `Randhex`, `SendSTD`, `ovhl7`) to launch DDoS attacks against specified targets. The malware also gathers network information by reading `/proc/net/route` in the `getOurIP` function.",
